# Biome CSS Lint Rule — Implementation Reference

Repository root is `/workspace/repo` (not `/workspace`). All paths below are absolute.

## Executive summary: how registration actually works

Biome scaffolds and registers new rules through **codegen**, not manual edits. The recommended flow is:

```
just new-css-lintrule myRuleName      # scaffolds files + registers category
just gen-analyzer                     # regenerates all the "Generated file, do not edit" files
```

`just new-css-lintrule` (justfile line 172) runs `cargo run -p xtask_codegen -- new-lintrule --kind=css --category=lint --name=<name>`, which invokes `generate_new_analyzer_rule` + `generate_analyzer_rule_options` (see `/workspace/repo/xtask/codegen/src/main.rs:80-87`). Then `just gen-analyzer` (justfile:47) regenerates the group/registry/config files.

The nursery group file uses **filesystem auto-discovery**, so the group registration is automatic once your `.rs` file exists. Details in section 4.

---

## 1. Nursery rules + representative examples

Directory `/workspace/repo/crates/biome_css_analyze/src/lint/nursery/`:
- `no_deprecated_media_type.rs`
- `no_duplicate_selectors.rs`
- `no_excessive_lines_per_file.rs`
- `no_hex_colors.rs`
- `use_baseline.rs`

No single nursery rule both uses a non-trivial custom Options struct *and* walks selectors, so here are two:

### (a) Rule with real custom options — `no_excessive_lines_per_file.rs`
Full content of `/workspace/repo/crates/biome_css_analyze/src/lint/nursery/no_excessive_lines_per_file.rs`:

```rust
use biome_analyze::{
    Ast, Rule, RuleDiagnostic, context::RuleContext, declare_lint_rule, utils::count_lines_in_file,
};
use biome_console::markup;
use biome_css_syntax::{CssRoot, CssSyntaxKind};
use biome_rowan::AstNode;
use biome_rule_options::no_excessive_lines_per_file::NoExcessiveLinesPerFileOptions;

declare_lint_rule! {
    /// Restrict the number of lines in a file.
    /// ... (doc comment with ```json,options``` and ```css,expect_diagnostic,use_options``` blocks) ...
    pub NoExcessiveLinesPerFile {
        version: "2.3.12",
        name: "noExcessiveLinesPerFile",
        language: "css",
        recommended: false,
    }
}

impl Rule for NoExcessiveLinesPerFile {
    type Query = Ast<CssRoot>;
    type State = usize;
    type Signals = Option<Self::State>;
    type Options = NoExcessiveLinesPerFileOptions;

    fn run(ctx: &RuleContext<Self>) -> Self::Signals {
        let node = ctx.query();
        let options = ctx.options();
        let file_lines_count = count_lines_in_file(
            node.syntax(),
            |token| token.kind() == CssSyntaxKind::EOF,
            options.skip_blank_lines(),
        );
        if file_lines_count > options.max_lines().get().into() {
            return Some(file_lines_count);
        }
        None
    }

    fn diagnostic(ctx: &RuleContext<Self>, state: &Self::State) -> Option<RuleDiagnostic> {
        let node = ctx.query();
        let options = ctx.options();
        Some(
            RuleDiagnostic::new(
                rule_category!(),
                node.range(),
                markup! {
                    "This file has too many lines ("{state}"). Maximum allowed is "{options.max_lines().to_string()}"."
                },
            )
            .note(markup! { "Consider splitting this file into smaller files." }),
        )
    }
}
```

Key takeaways: `type Options = <Name>Options;`, `ctx.options()` returns `&<Name>Options`, and option accessors (`.max_lines()`, `.skip_blank_lines()`) are hand-written on the options struct (section 3).

### (b) Rule that resolves/analyzes selectors — `no_duplicate_selectors.rs`
Full content of `/workspace/repo/crates/biome_css_analyze/src/lint/nursery/no_duplicate_selectors.rs` (abridged doc comment):

```rust
