## 2. Module registration file — `nursery.rs`

Full content of `/workspace/repo/crates/biome_css_analyze/src/lint/nursery.rs`:

```rust
//! Generated file, do not edit by hand, see `xtask/codegen`

#![doc = r" Group description generated by proc macro at compile time."]
#![doc = r""]
#![doc = r" To add a new rule, create a `.rs` file in the group subdirectory"]
#![doc = r" and run `cargo check`. The build system will automatically discover"]
#![doc = r" and register your rule."]
use biome_analyze_macros::declare_group_from_fs;
declare_group_from_fs! { category : "lint" , group : "nursery" }
```

**You do NOT edit this file.** `declare_group_from_fs!` scans the `nursery/` directory at compile time and registers every `.rs` file automatically (see the macro impl at `/workspace/repo/crates/biome_analyze_macros/src/group_macro.rs:52` — it reads the dir, PascalCases each file stem into the rule type, and emits `pub mod <name>;` + registration). The parent `lint.rs` (`/workspace/repo/crates/biome_css_analyze/src/lint.rs`) and `registry.rs` are likewise generated.

